  "body": "The placed DXF punch in #2978 accepts a circle or a racetrack. Extend it to one closed convex loop of tangent straight lines and circular arcs. This builds on the Wire Contour part of #2022.\n\nRead the actual curves from the DXF source. Check continuity, tangency, convexity, finite radius and the extent of every arc after placement. Preserve the nominal centers and winding in native output. Use a bounded conservative preview for the normal kerf and clearance checks. Require a clear threading lead and a straight section for separation.\n\nExercise more than one radius in the same sketch. Compare the placed arc centers and all pass radii with a fresh offline Agie Control plot. Reject a folded or intersecting loop, unsafe lead, short seam or a grid rounding change that makes a native arc invalid. Existing circle and racetrack jobs must retain their output.\n\nSuggested labels are P6, effort:high, area:post, area:2d, enhancement and source:agent.\n",
